// Version numbers for the app + widget targets. Both targets read this file, so
// bump values here — never in per-target build settings.
//
// MARKETING_VERSION is the user-facing version ("1.10" in the App Store).
//
// CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION is the build number. Info.plist resolves CFBundleVersion
// from $(CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION), so this value MUST stay defined — without it the
// build falls back to "1" from project.pbxproj and App Store Connect rejects the
// upload (build numbers must always increase).
//
// Who owns the build number:
//   - Xcode Cloud IGNORES this value and auto-increments from the highest build
//     already in App Store Connect. That is why shipped builds ran 20, 21, 22, 23
//     while this file still read 19.
//   - A manual archive from Xcode uses THIS value verbatim. (Until 2026-09-15 the
//     scheme had an Archive pre-action running `agvtool next-version -all`, which
//     ignored this file, bumped the *test* targets' numbers, and hardcoded
//     CFBundleVersion into Info.plist as a dirty working-tree change. Removed.)
//   - App Store Connect is authoritative for what actually shipped.
//
// So: after each release, set this to the last shipped build number — or the next
// one up if that number is already taken. That keeps a manual archive from
// colliding with a number Xcode Cloud has already used.
//
// Last shipped: v1.11, build 82, archived by Release Flow 2026-09-15 and the
// TestFlight / App Store candidate (build 77 the same day was superseded). The
// counter then reached 83 with the next PR's CI run — every workflow draws from
// the same sequence. Set to 84 so a manual archive cannot collide with a number
// already in App Store Connect.
MARKETING_VERSION = 1.11
CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION = 84
